# VIOLATION — this file MUST be rejected. It is not a bug; its rejection
# is the diode working as designed. Try it:
#   python -m jtv.cli examples/violation.jtv --mode control
# and observe a DataParseError, not a crash deep in evaluation.
#
# The assignment below tries to put a CONTROL if/then/else construct on
# the right-hand side of `=` — i.e. in DATA-grammar position. The DATA
# parser (data_parser.py) has no grammar production that accepts an `if`
# token; there is no rule anywhere in that file that would let this
# parse. Rejection happens at parse time, before any evaluation, because
# the two grammars are structurally separate: CONTROL has an `if_stmt`
# production, DATA does not, and the assignment's right-hand side is
# always parsed by the DATA parser, never the CONTROL parser.
begin
  x = if 1 < 2 then 3 else 4
end
